Subject: mysys: one shared descriptor per file on OpenVMS (my_vmsfile.c)

The OpenVMS C RTL buffers file data per descriptor: one that has written a
block keeps serving it from its own buffer and never sees writes made to
the file through another descriptor (vms-mariadb docs/DECISIONS.md D10).
MariaDB opens files several times. Like my_winfile.cc on Windows, route
mysys file I/O on VMS through my_vms_*() in the new mysys/my_vmsfile.c: one
master descriptor per file does all data I/O with pread()/pwrite(); each
my_open() descriptor keeps only its own position. File sizes come from
lseek(SEEK_END), since st_size is stale until fsync() or close().

